11. (Previously Presented) The control system of claim 8, wherein one of the first and second torque sources has a faster wheel torque response capability than the other, and when the first and second torque requests are changing in opposite directions and at least one of the corresponding torque requests is not satisfiable, the relative variation is dependent on the relationship:MTSINC-MTSDEC;wherein MTS refers to a torque rate modifier, wherein INC refers to the one of the first and second torque sources providing a positive rate of torque change, and wherein DEC refers to the other of the first and second torque sources providing a negative rate of torque change.-3- U.S.S.N. 17/920,770

